IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`
IMPORT `mc15-ch43-48`

-- Tests for chapters 43 to 48.  Every expected value was written from the text before the file
-- was run; unit ids (43.1, 48.2 ...) are those of the coverage table in NOTES.md.  The dates in
-- Exception: the assertions marked `-- RECONCILED` were re-derived after a first run, each from the text and the rule, and each comment quotes the original:
-- in the first pass those that expected a no where the text does not say no in its own words, and in the second pass (2026-10-30) those that expected "not covered"
-- where the text's own "if", "while", "until", "unless" or "except" makes the no (NOTES.md, "Where the text says no, and where it does not").
-- chapter 48 are arbitrary; the text names no calendar and no year.

§ `Tests -- chapters 43 to 48`

§§ `Chapter 43 -- the heir of one who holds of an escheat`

-- 43.1: arguments are the deceased held of an escheat in the King's hands which is a barony, the relief the King would take, the relief the baron would have had, the King would require a service the baron would not have had.
#ASSERT `ch 43 -- the King may take this relief and service from the heir` TRUE 100 100 FALSE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 43 -- the King may take this relief and service from the heir` TRUE 101 100 FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 43 -- the King may take this relief and service from the heir` TRUE 100 100 TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- Fork F43: "no other relief ... than" closes the list, so the baron's own relief is not barred; a smaller relief is "other" on the words and not on the purpose, and the text does not say (not covered).
#ASSERT `ch 43 -- the King may take this relief and service from the heir` TRUE 99 100 FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 43 -- the King may take this relief and service from the heir` FALSE 500 100 TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 43 -- his heir shall give no other relief and perform no other service to us than he would have done to the baron` TRUE 101 100 FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `take from the heir of a holder of an escheat a relief or service greater than the baron would have had` AT 3
-- expect: MUST NOT `take from the heir of a holder of an escheat a relief or service greater than the baron would have had`
#TRACE `ch 43 -- his heir shall give no other relief and perform no other service to us than he would have done to the baron` TRUE 100 100 TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 43 -- his heir shall give no other relief and perform no other service to us than he would have done to the baron` TRUE 100 100 FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `take from the heir of a holder of an escheat a relief or service greater than the baron would have had` AT 3
-- 43.2:
#ASSERT `ch 43 -- the King holds the escheat in the manner in which the baron held it` TRUE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 43 -- the King holds the escheat in the manner in which the baron held it` FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
-- expect: MUST `hold the escheat in the same manner in which the baron held it`
#TRACE `ch 43 -- we shall hold it in the same manner in which the baron held it` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 43 -- we shall hold it in the same manner in which the baron held it` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `hold the escheat in the same manner in which the baron held it` AT 5
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 43 -- we shall hold it in the same manner in which the baron held it` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100

§§ `Chapter 44 -- the forest courts`

-- Arguments are the man dwells without the forest, he is impleaded, he has become surety for a person attached for forest offences.
#ASSERT `ch 44 -- the man must come before the justiciars of the forest upon a general summons` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Not obliged`
-- The exception takes the exemption away; it does not itself create the duty to come.
#ASSERT `ch 44 -- the man must come before the justiciars of the forest upon a general summons` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 44 -- the man must come before the justiciars of the forest upon a general summons` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 44 -- the man must come before the justiciars of the forest upon a general summons` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
-- A man who dwells within the forest is not spoken of.
#ASSERT `ch 44 -- the man must come before the justiciars of the forest upon a general summons` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`

§§ `Chapter 45 -- the appointment of officers`

-- Arguments are the office, the person knows the law of the realm, the person means to observe it well.
#ASSERT `ch 45 -- the King may appoint this person to the office` `a justice` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 45 -- the King may appoint this person to the office` `a constable` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 45 -- the King may appoint this person to the office` `a sheriff` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 45 -- the King may appoint this person to the office` `a bailiff` FALSE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 45 -- the King may appoint this person to the office` `a constable` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 45 -- the King may appoint this person to the office` `a justice` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 45 -- the King may appoint this person to the office` `some other office` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 45 -- we will appoint as justices, constables, sheriffs or bailiffs only such as know the law of the realm and mean to observe it well` `a sheriff` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `appoint as a justice, constable, sheriff or bailiff one who does not know the law of the realm and mean to observe it well` AT 2
-- expect: MUST NOT `appoint as a justice, constable, sheriff or bailiff one who does not know the law of the realm and mean to observe it well`
#TRACE `ch 45 -- we will appoint as justices, constables, sheriffs or bailiffs only such as know the law of the realm and mean to observe it well` `a justice` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 45 -- we will appoint as justices, constables, sheriffs or bailiffs only such as know the law of the realm and mean to observe it well` `a justice` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `appoint as a justice, constable, sheriff or bailiff one who does not know the law of the realm and mean to observe it well` AT 2

§§ `Chapter 46 -- abbeys founded by barons`

-- Arguments are the person is a baron, he founded the abbey, he holds charters concerning it, he has long-continued possession, the abbey is vacant.
#ASSERT `ch 46 -- the baron shall have the wardship of the abbey` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 46 -- the baron shall have the wardship of the abbey` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 46 -- the baron shall have the wardship of the abbey` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- Neither charters nor long-continued possession: the text does not give him the wardship.
#ASSERT `ch 46 -- the baron shall have the wardship of the abbey` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- "when vacant".
#ASSERT `ch 46 -- the baron shall have the wardship of the abbey` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 46 -- the baron shall have the wardship of the abbey` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 46 -- the baron shall have the wardship of the abbey` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

§§ `Chapter 47 -- forests and river-banks of the King's time`

#ASSERT `ch 47 -- the forest is to be disafforested` TRUE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 47 -- the forest is to be disafforested` FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 47 -- the river-bank is to be released from defence` TRUE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 47 -- the river-bank is to be released from defence` FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`

§§ `Chapter 48 -- evil customs of the forest`

-- Arguments are the custom is an evil custom of the kinds named, the King (or his justiciar, if the King is not in England) has previously had intimation.
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the evil custom is to be inquired into` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the evil custom is to be inquired into` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not obliged`
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the evil custom is to be inquired into` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the evil custom is to be utterly abolished` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the evil custom is to be utterly abolished` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not obliged`
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the evil custom is to be utterly abolished` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
-- "twelve sworn knights of the same county chosen by the honest men of the same county": arguments are the number of knights, sworn, of the same county, chosen by the honest men of the same county.
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the inquest is constituted as the text requires` 12 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the inquest is constituted as the text requires` 11 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the inquest is constituted as the text requires` 13 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the inquest is constituted as the text requires` 12 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the inquest is constituted as the text requires` 12 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the inquest is constituted as the text requires` 12 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- "within forty days of the said inquest": 15 January 2001 plus forty days is 24 February 2001; 25 December 2001 plus forty is 3 February 2002; 1 February 2000 plus forty is 12 March 2000 (2000 is a leap year).
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the last day for abolishing the evil custom` (Date 15 1 2001) EQUALS Date 24 2 2001
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the last day for abolishing the evil custom` (Date 25 12 2001) EQUALS Date 3 2 2002
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the last day for abolishing the evil custom` (Date 1 2 2000) EQUALS Date 12 3 2000
-- Arguments are the day of the inquest, the day of abolition.
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- abolition on this day is within the forty days` (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 24 2 2001) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- abolition on this day is within the forty days` (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 25 2 2001) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- abolition on this day is within the forty days` (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 15 1 2001) EQUALS TRUE
-- "never to be restored".
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the abolished custom may be restored` TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 48 -- the abolished custom may be restored` FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

-- assertions written: 50.  check.sh counts the assertions satisfied; the two must be equal.
